// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 15 „Suhted, külaskäik ja viisakus” (a2-071…075), level A2, in the final shape
// (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_A2.md, row m15 = m7: PROB AVAS KUUL LUGU with the leads of modules 11–19; gates V1–V16 of
// docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B1.md §8). One storyline, one year before the B1 course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): June. Tom's neighbour Sandra Raud
// (flat 4; husband Ago) invites him for Saturday 12 June, his first visit to an Estonian home. Anna (seller at Kaubahall, boss Eha) goes to her
// sister on Hiiumaa from 18 to 21 June and has to ask for help: her neighbour Viktor, Sofia (summer shifts at Kaubahall), Eha. Viktor invites
// everybody to his farm for jaanipäev (Wednesday 23 June, from the Aegviidu train at 17.30). Tom gets off at Kehra and on the morning
// after he finds a wallet in the grass. Picture (art/visuals/a2-module-15.js): 072 Anna and Viktor in the corridor.
//   071 PROB L→S  the visit: Tule sisse! Võtke istet! Kas soovite kohvi? (osastav), Aitäh kutse eest!, Mul on aeg minna; first try, language, second
//                 try; corner L2 (a radio talk on visiting, true / false; after 069's W1); main: the visit, 2–3 minutes (S10); S05 = the second try.
//   072 AVAS R→S  polite requests: Palun + käsk, Kas sa saad …?, Kas te saate …?, Kas ma võin / tohin …?; try first → rule → try again;
//                 corner R1 (set phrases); main: the pair agrees who is asked what (S03); home recording: the picture (S06).
//   073 KUUL L→W  agreeing and refusing: Hea meelega!, Kahjuks ma ei saa, sest …, Aga kas … sobib?, Äkki …?; corner L1 (seven voice messages);
//                 main: a reply of 50–70 words (W08), planned first.
//   074 LUGU R→W  Tom's journey, a story with a cliffhanger; the message plan, Aitäh … eest!, Palun anna teada; corner W2a (the wallet);
//                 main: a message of 50–70 words to Viktor (W04), edited.
//   075 EKS       the module exam, every part timed (B.examPart): R1–R5, L1–L4, W1, W2a, S0, S1, S2.
// Every teaching lesson: „Mäletad?” naming the previous lesson and one of modules 11–13, an in-lesson pair task, a home recording in
// Kasuta, two fluency tasks, one exam corner. No tingiv kõneviis (A2): „Kas te saate …?”, „Äkki …?”, never „Kas te saaksite …?”, „Tahaksin …”, „Kuidas oleks …?”.
